# The bite (pitch bend): +-2 semitones by default, then the range set on the Pitch page
wait 200
midi 90 45 64
midi B0 02 7F
wait 20
expect note 6900
midi E0 7F 7F
wait 10
expect note 7100
midi E0 00 00
wait 10
expect note 6700
shot bite_down.png
midi E0 00 40
tap SEQ
expect view 12
spin K1 5
expect par8 7
midi E0 7F 7F
wait 10
expect note 7600
midi E0 00 40
midi 80 45 00
wait 100
# nothing on the screen is stale
wait 50
expect stale 0
# a bite too small to cross a tenth of a semitone still redraws the cents (+5c here; after the note,
# when nothing else on the screen moves)
midi 90 45 64
midi B0 02 7F
wait 30
expect notename A4
midi 80 45 00
midi B0 02 00
wait 1500
midi E0 3A 40
wait 50
expect note 6905
expect stale 0
# below MIDI 0 (note 0, bitten 7 down): the octave rounds down, F-2, not F-1
midi E0 00 40
midi 80 45 00
midi 90 00 64
midi E0 00 00
wait 30
expect note -700
expect notename F-2
midi E0 00 40
midi 80 00 00
midi B0 02 00
wait 200
